<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II, Count of Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1547">1547</a>–<a href="/years/1606">1606</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II, Count of Hohenzollern-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen">Sigmaringen</a>, was a son of Count Charles I of Hohenzollern. When his father's lands were divided in 1576 he received Sigmaringen and Veringen on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, founding the Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen line. His descendants were raised to princes in 1623 and later supplied the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-count-of-hohenzollern-sigmaringen.jpg" alt="Charles II, Count of Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_II_hohenzollern.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
